d he's a rookie Shaq pulls up  rolls down the window said where are you  going and he said to practice and he  said my teammates don't walk to practice  he opened up the glove compartment and  threw a wad of money at him and I said  five grand he goes no no he hit me  really hard probably 10 grand in cash  and told him to go get a car that right  there Shaquille O'Neal on a truck  actually back in the day for one of the  locker room attendants and so he could  he could kind of put the equipment and  in a pickup truck and stuff like that  for it just has that sense about him he  loves taking selfies with people I see  him down here in Manhattan Beach or  Hermosa Beach from time to time  he's on what we called strand here  that's kind of like the boardwalk right  right between these very expensive  houses and the water and Shaq will be  tooling up and down on a bicycle and he  looks like it's five sizes too small for  him and he does not care that is the as  you say the marketing genius of  Shaquille O'Neal he just had a doesn't  care and people really really respect  and adore him because of it is he who's  more beloved Kobe or Shaq Kobe and that  that's a great question Kobe was the  opposite he was the guy who was deathly  serious he's the one who wanted to  practice for at 6 a.m.  down in the Orange County in the month  of August with all the NBA is in the  Bahamas or in Vegas he's always the guy  who got up early and worked his ass off  and LA respected him for it and still  does and they feel like Shaq might have  clowned around a little too much I don't  think so I was appreciated that Shaq had  had flow with the media and he realized  he was getting paid millions upon  millions to be a player and an endorser  but but Kobe on the other hand he just  took everything so seriously and he won  and his drive really captivated the  Laker fan base here in LA and still does  to this day very much so Mike thanks for  joining us we appreciate your time we'll  check in with you during the season so  sad to hear your time in LA is there to  come back to you all right thank you  Mike Mike Bresnahan a Laker analyst for  Spectrum Sports Net you know the  brilliance of Shaq is that when he  endorses a product he buys he wants a  piece of the company you know the  general he gets a piece of that there's  a security system that he's involved in  I think he got a piece of the company  that's where you make some large cash  it's not just hey we're gonna pay you to  endorse this he wants he believes in the  product so much he wants a piece of it  and Jack's on his way to becoming a  billionaire for more Dan Patrick show  tune in the audience channel 239 on  DirecTV streamed for free on BR Live or  download the Dan Patrick show at  [Music]

